contentText:
Noah Kahan soundtracked an especially emotional &#8220;in memoriam&#8221; segment at the 2026 Primetime Emmy Awards on Monday night (Sept. 14), which was introduced by the movie and TV children of late actress Catherine O&#8217;Hara.

Home Alone star Macauley Culkin tearfully remembered how O&#8217;Hara showed up for him in life just like a real parent would after first portraying his mother in the 1990 Christmas classic. Then Schitt&#8217;s Creek stars Annie Murphy and Dan Levy both shared joyful memories of O&#8217;Hara on set as their quirky mother in the 2015-20 television comedy as well as sweet recollections of how strangers rallied around them in the wake of her death at age 71 in January.

