Following their intro, Kahan took the stage to perform Simon & Garfunkel &#8216;s &#8220;Bridge Over Troubled Water,&#8221; playing acoustic guitar and backed by a mournful string section. The folk duo&#8217;s 1970 six-week Billboard Hot 100 No. 1 hit has long soundtracked poignant moments, thanks to its sad-but-hopeful lyrics: &#8220;When darkness comes and pain is all around/ Like a bridge over troubled water, I will lay me down.&#8221;

Once Kahan finished his performance, Jamie Lee Curtis took the stage to pay tribute to Rob Reiner, the actor/director who first made a name for himself playing Michael &#8220;Meathead&#8221; Stivic on the 1970s sitcom All in the Family and was tragically murdered alongside his wife, Michelle, in December. Curtis sobbed throughout her remembrance to the Hollywood legend. &#8220;He was generous and kind and funny as hell and a friend to all.”

Noah Kahan performed during In Memoriam #Emmys pic.twitter.com/M1x1Vh1P23

&mdash; Enjoy The Music (@EnjoyTheMusic9) September 15, 2026

Earlier in the Emmys broadcast, there was a stand-alone tribute to Dolly Parton , who died last month of cancer at age 80. Sally Field, who co-starred with Parton in Steel Magnolias , introduced the tribute and Reba McEntire performed &#8220;Appalachian Memories.&#8221;
